WEBVTT

00:15.160 --> 00:16.500
Move! Be quick!

00:16.500 --> 00:17.260
Faster!

00:18.070 --> 00:18.570
You,

00:19.030 --> 00:19.800
move faster.

00:23.030 --> 00:24.290
You don't mess with me.

00:24.310 --> 00:26.330
[Deep in the Rainforest;
Warner Excavation Team]

00:30.460 --> 00:32.030
You, over there.

00:43.770 --> 00:45.550
[Hudson, Archaeological Team Leader]

00:44.250 --> 00:45.880
This damn forest isn't safe.

00:47.200 --> 00:49.130
There's something evil out there.

00:53.650 --> 00:55.920
Mr. Warner has had us

00:55.920 --> 00:56.880
digging here for months.

00:56.880 --> 00:58.030
When are we leaving?

00:57.340 --> 00:59.910
[Steven, Archaeological Team Clerk/Medic]

00:59.530 --> 01:02.030
We just wait for him
to find what he wants.

01:02.790 --> 01:04.840
These oriental lands are full of

01:04.840 --> 01:06.790
ancient and mystical artifacts—

01:07.200 --> 01:08.870
extremely valuable ones.

01:10.840 --> 01:12.150
God damn it.

01:12.789 --> 01:13.720
Hey, who are you?

01:14.070 --> 01:15.800
How the hell did you get in here?

01:15.950 --> 01:16.500
Wait...

01:16.760 --> 01:18.620
Why is she carrying severed arms?

01:38.870 --> 01:40.140
Black magic curse!

01:46.840 --> 01:47.650
Who are you?

02:01.260 --> 02:02.460
May you rest in peace.

02:12.080 --> 02:13.910
I wanna talk with the boss here

02:14.580 --> 02:15.650
about a deal.

02:24.340 --> 02:24.970
Miss Dong,

02:25.410 --> 02:26.870
could you repeat that, please?

02:26.870 --> 02:28.530
What do you want me to help you?

02:28.840 --> 02:31.300
I need someone to
escort me back to Xiacheng.

02:31.690 --> 02:33.870
Otherwise, I'll die on the way.

02:34.250 --> 02:36.600
[Warner, Professor/Explorer]

02:34.650 --> 02:36.310
We're just an expedition team

02:36.340 --> 02:38.740
here to study
East Asian culture and rocks.

02:38.800 --> 02:40.650
We don't engage in this kind of business.

02:40.650 --> 02:42.000
Why come to the jungle

02:42.030 --> 02:44.340
to ask our expedition for help?

02:45.579 --> 02:46.500
Because

02:47.300 --> 02:48.750
I need your faces.

02:49.530 --> 02:50.650
Our faces?

02:51.000 --> 02:51.620
Yes.

02:52.650 --> 02:53.530
Those people can steal

02:53.530 --> 02:55.840
others' faces to approach me.

02:56.370 --> 02:59.960
Well, the faces of foreigners
like you guys

03:00.300 --> 03:02.760
are much more difficult
for them to imitate.

03:07.910 --> 03:10.640
It seems the South Seas are
full of strange tales.

03:11.340 --> 03:12.300
As a reward,

03:13.030 --> 03:14.560
I can give you what you seek.

03:16.030 --> 03:17.840
Things cannot be found here.

03:26.030 --> 03:27.800
How did you get this map?

03:28.530 --> 03:29.150
Deal.

03:30.750 --> 03:32.410
Let's get ready for boarding.

04:58.900 --> 05:04.980
[Archives: The Nanyang Mystery]

05:05.350 --> 05:08.070
[Episode 4]

05:12.450 --> 05:14.160
Then I'll start
forcing information out of you.

05:14.160 --> 05:15.370
Answer my questions,

05:16.190 --> 05:17.920
or I'm going to crush his spine,

05:18.040 --> 05:19.540
vertebra by vertebra.

05:20.120 --> 05:21.850
For every minute you hesitate,

05:22.750 --> 05:24.160
I'll crush one more.

05:24.680 --> 05:26.550
Right now, he can still feel his hands.

05:26.550 --> 05:27.770
In seven minutes,

05:28.120 --> 05:29.420
other than his head...

05:30.790 --> 05:31.440
No.

05:32.370 --> 05:34.420
He'll only be able to move his head.

05:36.250 --> 05:38.000
No, I'll tell you right now!

05:44.500 --> 05:46.560
You're not putting up much of a fight.

05:49.040 --> 05:51.240
We civilian experts are not exactly...

05:51.330 --> 05:53.460
not exactly sticklers for principle.

05:54.690 --> 05:55.659
So then,

05:56.190 --> 05:57.590
the toxic weed in Xucheng

05:58.360 --> 06:00.290
was indeed planted deliberately.

06:02.330 --> 06:04.250
I investigated it three years ago.

06:04.250 --> 06:06.370
The plant was believed to have gone extinct
during the Ming Dynasty.

06:06.370 --> 06:08.220
And Panhua Reef—
the only place where its seeds

06:08.220 --> 06:09.800
had ever been found—was blown up.

06:09.800 --> 06:10.690
So, in this world, the only people

06:10.690 --> 06:12.120
who still possessed Twilight Grass

06:12.120 --> 06:14.450
were those warlords from three years ago.

06:16.540 --> 06:18.570
After the poison broke out
in the three villages in Xucheng,

06:18.570 --> 06:20.190
the toxic weed began appearing

06:20.190 --> 06:21.790
in 15 villages across Balai.

06:22.330 --> 06:23.500
But by then,

06:23.570 --> 06:25.300
I had already grown suspicious

06:25.300 --> 06:27.500
and stationed people in every village.

06:27.800 --> 06:29.500
The source of the poison
was quickly dealt with,

06:29.500 --> 06:31.230
and the outbreak never spread.

06:32.110 --> 06:33.300
You mean

06:33.370 --> 06:35.970
this poisoning was aimed at
the whole of Balai,

06:36.120 --> 06:37.750
and they simply chose Xucheng first?

06:37.750 --> 06:40.000
Xucheng was simply the first
to see an outbreak

06:40.000 --> 06:41.450
because it's the closest city to the port.

06:41.450 --> 06:43.000
But fortunately, I had people stationed

06:43.000 --> 06:45.450
in the surrounding villages
and mountain passes.

06:45.450 --> 06:47.420
So your Balongzhou was spared.

06:48.300 --> 06:49.270
I did lose

06:49.420 --> 06:51.220
quite a few of my people, though.

06:51.540 --> 06:54.340
I won't let whoever is behind this
get away with it.

06:57.750 --> 06:59.070
Mr. Zhang Ruipu,

06:59.100 --> 07:00.690
since you're so resourceful—

07:00.690 --> 07:03.090
able to uncover our backgrounds so quickly

07:03.690 --> 07:05.370
and stop the poisonings—

07:05.620 --> 07:07.950
have you identified the people behind it?

07:15.800 --> 07:17.120
Look at these 15 villages—

07:16.460 --> 07:23.350
[Langhuacheng] [Yungangyi] [Yeruicheng]

07:17.690 --> 07:19.660
they're evenly spread across
the entire coast.

07:19.660 --> 07:22.300
And the first three poisoned villages
in Xucheng

07:22.300 --> 07:23.040
are here.

07:23.660 --> 07:25.690
I connected them according to the order

07:25.690 --> 07:27.300
in which the poison outbreaks occurred

07:27.300 --> 07:28.870
and discovered
that they form a shipping route.

07:28.080 --> 07:30.200
[Balai Map]

07:29.300 --> 07:30.300
The timing of the outbreaks

07:30.300 --> 07:31.900
matches the travel schedule

07:32.190 --> 07:33.650
along that route exactly.

07:33.960 --> 07:37.130
[Xucheng] [Poisoned on the Nan'an]
[Xiacheng]

07:34.120 --> 07:35.040
The first outbreaks

07:35.040 --> 07:37.300
of Twilight Grass poisoning occurred
simultaneously in these three villages.

07:37.300 --> 07:38.430
And in each village,

07:39.010 --> 07:40.570
the very first poisoning victim

07:40.570 --> 07:42.159
arrived in Balai

07:42.330 --> 07:44.420
aboard the Nan'an from Xiacheng
during the first week of July.

07:42.370 --> 07:44.900
[Time of Poisoning]
[First Poisoning Victim] [July 2]

07:46.300 --> 07:47.250
It was this ship,

07:47.500 --> 07:48.190
the Nan'an.

07:49.159 --> 07:51.540
The poisoning victims
in Xucheng's three villages

07:51.540 --> 07:53.600
had also come ashore from the Nan'an.

07:53.950 --> 07:54.659
That

07:55.500 --> 07:56.900
also confirms my theory.

08:00.830 --> 08:02.570
It really is the Nan'an.

08:04.380 --> 08:06.210
If the Twilight Grass poisoning

08:06.690 --> 08:08.950
was indeed the work of the warlords,
as you say,

08:08.950 --> 08:10.880
the one thing that remains unclear

08:11.120 --> 08:12.420
is their motive.

08:14.330 --> 08:15.370
In that case,

08:16.070 --> 08:17.800
why not just send someone
aboard the Nan'an

08:17.800 --> 08:18.870
to investigate?

08:19.920 --> 08:21.540
That's exactly why I've come.

08:21.540 --> 08:22.570
My clansmen and I swore,

08:22.570 --> 08:24.420
after leaving the Southern Archives,

08:24.420 --> 08:25.250
that we would

08:25.800 --> 08:27.260
never return to Xiacheng.

08:27.450 --> 08:30.190
But someone has to help me
investigate this matter.

08:30.190 --> 08:31.500
Although personnel from the Archives

08:31.500 --> 08:33.030
are required to
undergo poison-resistance training,

08:33.030 --> 08:35.409
the Twilight Grass is
exceptionally deadly.

08:35.409 --> 08:37.070
I still lost many of my people.

08:37.750 --> 08:39.909
But you were exposed to Twilight Grass

08:40.080 --> 08:40.880
and survived.

08:41.409 --> 08:42.030
That's why

08:42.580 --> 08:43.750
I came to you.

08:43.860 --> 08:46.370
[Invitation; Nan'an]

08:44.410 --> 08:46.270
Here is your payment and a ticket.

08:46.340 --> 08:47.740
In three days, the Nan'an

08:47.910 --> 08:49.440
will be departing from here

08:49.700 --> 08:51.410
and heading straight for Xiacheng.

08:51.410 --> 08:53.270
Go on board to investigate for me,

08:53.750 --> 08:55.150
and I will help you take care of

08:55.150 --> 08:56.350
this friend of yours.

08:57.290 --> 08:58.750
If you can't find anything

08:59.120 --> 09:00.700
within half a year,

09:02.030 --> 09:03.080
your friend

09:03.790 --> 09:06.590
will become fertilizer
for my rubber plantation.

09:21.770 --> 09:26.260
[First-Class Cabin Ticket Stub]

09:21.870 --> 09:23.870
You can have us killed at any moment,

09:24.620 --> 09:26.550
so what you're saying must be true.

09:29.180 --> 09:30.530
I have one additional condition.

09:30.530 --> 09:31.080
Go ahead.

09:32.030 --> 09:32.870
My friend here

09:33.650 --> 09:35.840
needs to rinse his mouth
with shark-fin soup every morning.

09:35.840 --> 09:37.830
For lunch,
he needs eight dishes and a soup.

09:37.830 --> 09:39.200
Dinner can be a bit lighter—

09:39.200 --> 09:40.620
five dishes and plain congee.

09:40.620 --> 09:41.370
But the congee

09:41.370 --> 09:42.830
must have diced Jinhua ham

09:42.910 --> 09:44.510
and cordyceps flowers in it.

09:44.700 --> 09:47.200
As for his legs,
massage them three times a day.

09:47.200 --> 09:49.000
And he's afraid to sleep alone at night.

09:49.000 --> 09:50.340
You'd better find several girls

09:50.340 --> 09:51.340
to sleep with him.

09:59.500 --> 10:00.960
Were you, by any chance...

10:01.840 --> 10:03.840
raised by a woman named Zhang Haiqi?

10:05.500 --> 10:07.500
What's your relationship with her?

10:08.340 --> 10:09.750
You can go ask her yourself.

10:09.750 --> 10:10.370
And as for

10:10.650 --> 10:11.650
your friend here,

10:11.840 --> 10:13.700
I'll take even better care of him.

10:30.640 --> 10:32.650
Isn't the ticket for three days from now?

10:32.650 --> 10:34.250
It's docked ahead of schedule.

10:34.250 --> 10:35.460
My people will take you there.

10:35.460 --> 10:36.960
What a strange smell.

10:56.120 --> 10:57.030
I'll be back.

10:59.120 --> 11:02.050
Boss, will he really get on the ship
and investigate?

11:02.700 --> 11:03.790
A clever person

11:04.370 --> 11:06.290
always focuses on
solving practical problems—

11:06.290 --> 11:08.420
finding a chance to rescue his friend—

11:11.150 --> 11:13.480
rather than following the rules of a deal.

11:15.030 --> 11:16.030
On his way there,

11:16.500 --> 11:17.460
someone

11:18.290 --> 11:20.460
will make the stakes very clear to him.

11:23.410 --> 11:24.120
Haijiao.

11:24.910 --> 11:26.440
You're wearing a gardenia?

11:27.500 --> 11:29.670
The uncle who just took me outside
gave it to me.

11:29.670 --> 11:30.800
Flowers suit girls.

11:31.700 --> 11:33.960
Go play at Granny's next door for a while.

11:34.120 --> 11:34.750
No.

11:37.910 --> 11:39.460
I want to stay with you, Uncle Shrimpie,

11:39.460 --> 11:40.590
and take care of you.

11:42.290 --> 11:43.030
Little one,

11:44.410 --> 11:45.610
let me take both of you

11:45.750 --> 11:46.950
to my place as guests.

11:59.080 --> 12:00.000
From here on, your friend

12:00.000 --> 12:01.870
will be taken away
from the Southern Archives branch.

12:01.870 --> 12:03.870
We will erase every trace of his presence.

12:03.870 --> 12:04.580
If

12:04.910 --> 12:07.500
you slip off the ship after boarding
and come back here,

12:07.500 --> 12:08.870
you'll find only an empty room.

12:08.870 --> 12:09.500
Of course,

12:09.620 --> 12:11.290
we also have our men on the ship.

12:11.290 --> 12:13.030
If you dare disembark without permission,

12:13.030 --> 12:14.530
a telegram will be sent back immediately.

12:14.530 --> 12:15.870
Then, your friend

12:16.150 --> 12:18.750
will be beheaded,
and his head hung from a pole.

12:20.650 --> 12:22.840
Don't bother with petty tricks like that.

12:22.840 --> 12:24.160
By the time we got here,

12:24.290 --> 12:25.550
they had already left.

12:25.830 --> 12:27.760
And my boss's men are watching you.

12:27.790 --> 12:30.150
You'll always be watched.

12:30.530 --> 12:33.390
If you do anything
unrelated to the investigation,

12:33.790 --> 12:34.650
your friend

12:35.530 --> 12:36.500
will die.

12:47.530 --> 12:49.020
Leaving Shrimpie with you for half a year

12:49.020 --> 12:49.900
is too long.

12:51.000 --> 12:52.870
If I can find out the truth in three days,

12:52.870 --> 12:54.070
who should I contact?

12:54.460 --> 12:56.320
You'll know once you're on board.

12:57.460 --> 12:59.290
And if I happen to die on the ship,

13:00.340 --> 13:01.740
will you let Shrimpie go?

13:06.960 --> 13:07.530
Move.

13:21.340 --> 13:23.500
A sudden outbreak of toxic weed in Balai

13:23.500 --> 13:25.340
has left nearly a hundred casualties.

13:24.490 --> 13:27.340
[Emergency Notice]

13:39.060 --> 13:41.820
[Golden Needle—Special Equipment
of the Archives; Voice Modulation]

13:53.500 --> 13:54.620
The Nan'an...

15:37.460 --> 15:38.500
Nice weather today.

15:38.500 --> 15:39.580
Isn't it always?

15:40.790 --> 15:42.250
Watch where you're going!

15:42.620 --> 15:43.410
Sorry.

16:00.370 --> 16:01.150
Mr. Zhang,

16:01.530 --> 16:03.260
are you getting on board or not?

16:05.060 --> 16:07.410
[Invitation; Nan'an]

16:05.790 --> 16:07.250
Tell Zhang Ruipu for me

16:07.530 --> 16:09.330
that he'd better treat my friend

16:10.080 --> 16:12.340
with the same generosity he has shown me.

16:12.620 --> 16:14.250
We're just doing our jobs.

16:14.580 --> 16:16.750
Whether Mr. Zhang Ruipu is generous or not

16:16.750 --> 16:17.700
is beyond our control.

16:17.700 --> 16:18.370
So,

16:18.870 --> 16:20.340
you'd better get moving.

16:36.000 --> 16:38.000
Alright, let's check your luggage.

16:44.580 --> 16:46.340
Sorry, a moment.

16:47.410 --> 16:48.250
Sorry.

16:53.700 --> 16:54.790
Hello, Mr. Zhang.

16:54.840 --> 16:56.370
You must be Mr. Zhang Hailou,

16:56.370 --> 16:57.830
Mr. Zhang Ruipu's nephew.

16:58.460 --> 17:01.120
I've been assigned specifically
to assist you.

17:06.109 --> 17:08.790
So you know everything
he's sent me to investigate?

17:08.790 --> 17:09.390
Of course.

17:09.609 --> 17:11.940
I'll do everything in my power
to help you.

17:14.650 --> 17:16.470
[Nan'an]

17:15.400 --> 17:17.220
Tell me about this ship first.

17:20.160 --> 17:21.700
On this route, the Nan'an

17:21.700 --> 17:23.240
is an absolute behemoth.

17:23.589 --> 17:24.880
She has an enormous capacity—

17:24.880 --> 17:27.349
able to hold at least 1,500 passengers.

17:27.369 --> 17:28.440
The crew alone

17:28.470 --> 17:30.010
numbers 437.

17:30.900 --> 17:31.940
Like other ships,

17:31.940 --> 17:33.340
she has three classes of cabins:

17:33.340 --> 17:35.580
first, second, and third.

17:37.790 --> 17:38.590
Essentially,

17:39.050 --> 17:40.750
the first and second classes

17:39.370 --> 17:42.830
[First-Class Cabin] [Second-Class Cabin]
[Corridor]

17:40.750 --> 17:41.950
are interconnected,

17:42.940 --> 17:44.640
but the third class is different.

17:43.450 --> 17:45.370
[Third-Class Cabin]

17:44.640 --> 17:47.300
Its activity areas
are relatively restricted.

17:47.720 --> 17:50.250
The ocean brings out
the crazy side in people.

17:51.830 --> 17:54.290
These people may
behave themselves on land,

17:54.530 --> 17:56.990
but once on board,
they let go of everything.

18:00.180 --> 18:01.940
Couldn't that make you catch something?

18:01.940 --> 18:03.500
There are doctors on board.

18:03.830 --> 18:05.690
Any issues can be brought to them.

18:07.440 --> 18:08.940
They treat third-class passengers too?

18:08.940 --> 18:09.770
Of course.

18:15.890 --> 18:17.230
How do you write "cabin" again?

18:17.230 --> 18:18.690
I've suddenly forgotten.

18:21.790 --> 18:23.240
Have you ever heard

18:23.260 --> 18:25.450
of anyone on this ship
being poisoned by Twilight Grass?

18:25.450 --> 18:28.310
I've never heard of anyone
being poisoned on board.

18:30.070 --> 18:31.000
Okay, thank you.

18:32.760 --> 18:33.840
This is weird.

18:33.860 --> 18:35.070
Zhang Ruipu said

18:35.500 --> 18:38.730
the Twilight Grass poisoning originated with
passengers disembarking from the ship,

18:38.730 --> 18:40.830
yet no one on board was poisoned.

18:40.850 --> 18:43.180
That's for you to investigate, I suppose.

18:44.600 --> 18:46.270
Have you ever seen

18:46.300 --> 18:47.660
any warlords or soldiers on board,

18:47.660 --> 18:48.850
wearing uniforms like this

18:48.850 --> 18:50.980
and carrying top-notch foreign guns?

18:53.160 --> 18:54.620
Why is there so much stuff?

18:54.630 --> 18:56.720
What do those have to do
with the people I'm looking for?

18:56.720 --> 18:57.960
Those are all mercenaries.

18:57.960 --> 18:59.020
When on shore,

18:59.050 --> 19:01.730
they looked a lot like
the warlords you described.

19:01.730 --> 19:03.060
But now that they're aboard,

19:03.060 --> 19:04.330
they must have changed into plain clothes.

19:04.330 --> 19:05.920
The luggage they're carrying

19:05.920 --> 19:07.450
is full of submachine guns.

19:07.950 --> 19:09.080
Move it, move it.

19:14.540 --> 19:16.600
Are they the ones you're looking for?

19:19.790 --> 19:20.500
Mr. Zhang?

19:20.990 --> 19:21.920
Deep in thought?

19:25.920 --> 19:27.260
That's the ship owner's daughter,

19:27.260 --> 19:27.980
Miss Dong,

19:28.300 --> 19:29.430
our young mistress.

19:33.680 --> 19:35.510
She was staying elsewhere,
passed through Balai,

19:35.510 --> 19:37.370
and is now taking her family's own ship
back to Xiacheng.

19:37.370 --> 19:38.220
Thanks to her,

19:38.240 --> 19:39.120
all the food on the ship

19:39.120 --> 19:40.420
is European wine and cured meat

19:40.420 --> 19:42.210
shipped from Balai's harbor warehouse.

19:42.210 --> 19:43.620
She's friends with those foreigners?

19:43.620 --> 19:44.690
Of course.

19:44.980 --> 19:46.260
Otherwise, how could Mr. Warner

19:46.260 --> 19:48.060
have brought firearms on board?

19:50.400 --> 19:51.200
What's wrong?

20:16.940 --> 20:19.470
Miss Dong doesn't look like someone
you want to mess with.

20:19.470 --> 20:20.800
We're all afraid of her.

20:21.320 --> 20:22.980
You'd better not provoke her.

20:23.980 --> 20:25.520
Tell me, if I control her,

20:25.550 --> 20:26.410
does that mean I

20:26.440 --> 20:27.930
indirectly control the whole ship?

20:27.930 --> 20:30.590
Wouldn't that speed up
the investigation considerably?

20:30.590 --> 20:31.700
What are you planning to do?

20:31.700 --> 20:32.630
Hijack the ship.

20:32.640 --> 20:33.970
Are you out of your mind?

20:57.070 --> 20:59.360
We have a tail, left side.

21:22.650 --> 21:25.300
If it were Shrimpie,
he definitely wouldn't hijack the ship.

21:25.300 --> 21:27.330
I have to find a way
to use Miss Dong's authority

21:27.330 --> 21:30.590
to track down
whoever's spreading Twilight Grass aboard.

21:56.510 --> 21:57.280
Hey, bro,

21:57.700 --> 21:59.430
maybe you're in the wrong seat.

22:01.480 --> 22:02.360
Miss Dong,

22:03.650 --> 22:05.590
you're in serious danger right now.

22:05.590 --> 22:06.770
But I can help you.

22:07.860 --> 22:08.600
Miss Dong,

22:09.250 --> 22:11.110
would you like me to throw him off?

22:12.090 --> 22:14.140
With your skills, Mr. Hudson,

22:14.850 --> 22:17.780
you may not be able to
throw him overboard.

22:18.330 --> 22:20.840
Plus, he's a first-class passenger.

22:23.230 --> 22:24.540
See him about it.

22:27.220 --> 22:28.920
Explain what you just said.

22:34.980 --> 22:35.810
Miss Dong.

22:40.630 --> 22:42.940
I can see you're the kind of person
who avoids drawing attention

22:42.940 --> 22:44.540
and keeps a very low profile.

22:45.310 --> 22:46.640
But if I'm not mistaken,

22:46.700 --> 22:47.860
you must have

22:47.890 --> 22:49.110
something very valuable on this ship

22:49.110 --> 22:51.570
that you're transporting back to Xiacheng.

22:52.030 --> 22:53.290
Looks like I was right.

22:53.720 --> 22:56.180
That's why you're sailing
on your own vessel

22:56.200 --> 22:57.200
and have secretly arranged

22:57.200 --> 22:59.200
so many guards to protect yourself.

23:02.130 --> 23:02.930
To be honest,

23:03.060 --> 23:04.710
I didn't actually guess any of that.

23:04.710 --> 23:07.020
Rather, I happened to overhear

23:07.720 --> 23:09.310
a group of people

23:10.490 --> 23:13.890
in a small tavern on shore
plotting to seize those valuables.

23:14.110 --> 23:15.170
But don't worry.

23:15.550 --> 23:16.680
I've got their faces

23:17.810 --> 23:19.980
burned into my memory.

23:22.010 --> 23:22.700
And then?

23:23.350 --> 23:25.320
Then, out of professional integrity

23:25.320 --> 23:27.180
and my deep hatred of wrongdoing,

23:28.250 --> 23:29.650
I've decided to help you.

23:30.220 --> 23:32.210
Miss Dong, today is your lucky day.

23:32.670 --> 23:33.670
I can protect you.

23:35.490 --> 23:36.770
I forgot to introduce myself.

23:36.770 --> 23:37.460
On the surface,

23:37.460 --> 23:38.900
I'm just a first-class passenger,

23:38.900 --> 23:39.700
but actually,

23:41.340 --> 23:42.470
I am a patrolman.

23:45.430 --> 23:46.910
It's just that my trip this time

23:46.910 --> 23:48.450
was arranged rather suddenly.

23:48.450 --> 23:50.220
So I might need to...

23:50.630 --> 23:52.430
So you need to borrow my men

23:53.240 --> 23:55.240
and have me give you full access

23:55.410 --> 23:57.470
to make things easier for you, right?

24:02.230 --> 24:04.030
Miss Dong, you're indeed sharp.

24:10.020 --> 24:11.220
With all due respect,

24:11.410 --> 24:13.470
even with all the men you've brought,

24:14.190 --> 24:16.250
in my opinion, it still isn't enough.

24:16.610 --> 24:17.760
You can rest assured.

24:17.760 --> 24:19.100
As a professional patrolman,

24:19.100 --> 24:20.190
I never lie.

24:21.870 --> 24:23.880
Besides, you won't lose anything anyway.

24:23.880 --> 24:25.110
What if I'm telling the truth, right?

24:25.110 --> 24:27.040
You sound so convincing right now.

24:28.070 --> 24:30.200
But if you don't find anyone in the end,

24:31.730 --> 24:33.460
how will you explain yourself?

24:35.060 --> 24:36.560
If I don't find anyone,

24:36.590 --> 24:37.590
then I can only...

24:39.160 --> 24:41.290
punish myself with three cups of wine.

24:42.480 --> 24:43.690
After all, that wouldn't be my fault.

24:43.690 --> 24:44.640
It could only mean...

24:44.640 --> 24:45.210
I understand.

24:45.210 --> 24:45.810
Tavern...

24:46.090 --> 24:46.890
I understand.

24:47.090 --> 24:48.890
You're just using that story as an excuse

24:48.890 --> 24:50.750
to get special privileges from me

24:50.750 --> 24:52.030
so you can investigate

24:52.060 --> 24:53.820
whatever it is
you're actually here to investigate,

24:53.820 --> 24:54.410
right?

24:55.130 --> 24:56.980
-Miss Dong, actually...
-Alright.

24:56.980 --> 24:58.810
Whatever your real motive may be,

24:58.810 --> 25:02.210
in keeping with the principle
that safety comes first at sea,

25:02.580 --> 25:04.240
I will give you the privilege.

25:05.010 --> 25:06.810
But I'm only giving you two days.

25:07.120 --> 25:08.980
If you haven't found those people

25:08.980 --> 25:10.710
before the ship departs in two days,

25:10.710 --> 25:13.250
I'll exercise my right as the ship owner

25:14.100 --> 25:18.050
and have you arrested
for seriously disrupting public order

25:18.290 --> 25:19.420
aboard this vessel—

25:20.150 --> 25:21.890
and sent to prison in Xiacheng.

25:22.070 --> 25:23.460
If you resist arrest,

25:23.490 --> 25:24.690
I'll authorize my men

25:25.080 --> 25:26.410
to shoot you on the spot.

25:26.990 --> 25:28.060
Do you accept?

25:31.020 --> 25:32.550
You have 10 seconds to answer me.

25:32.550 --> 25:33.310
I accept.

25:35.630 --> 25:37.310
And what if I find all those people?

25:37.310 --> 25:38.620
Find them first.

25:38.700 --> 25:39.370
Steven.

25:41.280 --> 25:42.240
He'll accompany you

25:42.240 --> 25:43.500
and open doors for you.

25:44.410 --> 25:46.990
You will have free rein on this ship

25:47.010 --> 25:48.410
and do whatever you want.

25:54.810 --> 25:57.280
Miss Dong seems to be...

26:00.020 --> 26:01.090
quite something.

26:01.760 --> 26:04.170
I'm Miss Dong's personal physician

26:05.130 --> 26:06.440
and also the quickest draw

26:06.440 --> 26:07.680
in Nanyang.

26:08.500 --> 26:09.840
How may I address you?

26:10.210 --> 26:11.340
What a coincidence.

26:11.560 --> 26:13.750
I'm the fastest blade in Nanyang.

26:16.410 --> 26:18.100
We can have a friendly spar.

26:18.410 --> 26:19.270
Let's use...

26:24.210 --> 26:26.140
Indeed, fast enough.

26:32.880 --> 26:33.930
So fast.

26:37.040 --> 26:38.390
But being too fast...

26:39.600 --> 26:41.350
isn't always a good thing.

26:42.680 --> 26:43.880
My last name is Zhang.

26:44.780 --> 26:46.310
I think we really hit it off.

26:46.320 --> 26:47.350
The next few days should be...

26:47.350 --> 26:50.080
Mr. Zhang, I'm going back to my cabin
to settle in.

26:51.010 --> 26:53.400
Let's meet here again in an hour.

26:53.960 --> 26:55.950
I'll officially start the clock then.

26:55.950 --> 26:57.780
Within 48 hours,

26:58.280 --> 27:01.470
you must find those bandits you mentioned.

27:01.650 --> 27:02.450
Otherwise...

27:12.340 --> 27:13.170
Interesting.

27:16.580 --> 27:17.340
Steven.

27:20.920 --> 27:22.090
Mr. Warner said

27:22.110 --> 27:25.300
we cannot let anything or anyone
delay the Nan'an's departure,

27:25.300 --> 27:27.710
including that voice-changing witch.

27:27.740 --> 27:30.780
Escorting Miss Dong is not our real objective,
so don't take her words to heart.

27:30.780 --> 27:31.510
Understood.

27:31.980 --> 27:32.780
Also,

27:33.430 --> 27:35.850
that man isn't important.

27:35.870 --> 27:37.030
You can let him be for now.

27:37.030 --> 27:38.640
But if he tries to interfere with it

27:38.640 --> 27:40.730
or do anything out of line,

27:40.750 --> 27:41.750
you just kill him.

27:58.190 --> 27:59.100
Take that road.

28:01.290 --> 28:02.660
This road is too narrow.

28:03.710 --> 28:04.910
I don't like it.

28:07.060 --> 28:08.290
I'm kidnapping you,

28:09.130 --> 28:11.460
yet you're acting like we're old friends.

28:13.090 --> 28:14.050
No need to worry.

28:14.480 --> 28:15.480
These flies...

28:16.320 --> 28:18.060
have been buzzing around me
for a long time.

28:18.060 --> 28:19.920
I'm quite good at swatting flies.

28:22.680 --> 28:24.280
I've lived here for 10 years.

28:24.760 --> 28:26.430
I know which route is shorter.

28:28.140 --> 28:30.400
Besides, my body can't handle the bumps.

28:31.000 --> 28:32.130
Please bear with me.

28:40.940 --> 28:41.480
Allow me.

28:53.990 --> 28:55.850
Your friend is quite impressive.

28:56.270 --> 28:57.870
A little impulsive, though.

28:58.830 --> 29:00.090
But you're different—

29:00.730 --> 29:01.490
calm

29:02.180 --> 29:02.790
and sharp.

29:04.090 --> 29:05.520
Why not come

29:05.550 --> 29:06.630
work for me

29:06.920 --> 29:08.330
and leave the Southern Archives?

29:08.330 --> 29:10.240
Mr. Zhang, you have
so many capable people around you.

29:10.240 --> 29:12.630
What use would you have
for a paralyzed man like me?

29:12.630 --> 29:13.890
I can't even swat a fly.

29:16.020 --> 29:16.980
As for you,

29:17.650 --> 29:19.680
I think you're in serious trouble.

29:19.700 --> 29:21.760
I've always been trouble for others.

29:22.100 --> 29:23.760
Everyone who dares to cross me

29:23.780 --> 29:24.930
never ends well.

29:25.640 --> 29:27.110
This time will be no different.

29:27.110 --> 29:28.410
Mr. Zhang, have you already

29:28.410 --> 29:30.090
figured out the truth behind this?

29:30.090 --> 29:31.890
I'm no longer with the Archives.

29:32.290 --> 29:33.780
I simply don't like...

29:34.870 --> 29:36.930
people disturbing my peaceful life.

29:37.320 --> 29:38.910
My friend is a lot like you.

29:39.150 --> 29:40.550
You're both very strong.

29:40.950 --> 29:42.440
But no matter how strong someone is,

29:42.440 --> 29:44.590
they might just die because of it.

29:48.960 --> 29:51.090
You're about to make your move, right?

30:13.090 --> 30:14.690
It's Twilight Grass Poison.

30:16.030 --> 30:18.370
The toxic weed incidents are connected to
the people who tried to kill you.

30:18.370 --> 30:19.850
Is Hailou in danger then?

30:22.070 --> 30:23.670
Just as I thought.

30:24.690 --> 30:25.990
Their target

30:26.240 --> 30:27.010
is Zhang...

30:44.980 --> 30:45.980
Where is Haijiao?

30:48.700 --> 30:50.110
Dead.

32:47.710 --> 32:48.430
One.

32:49.140 --> 32:49.780
Two.

32:50.890 --> 32:51.670
Three.

32:52.130 --> 32:52.750
Four.

32:54.480 --> 32:55.190
Five.

32:57.850 --> 32:58.530
Six.

33:05.730 --> 33:06.590
Follow him.
